<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasan-Jalal Dawla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1261</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Hasan-Jalal Vakhtangian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasan-Jalal Dawla was the Armenian prince of Khachen, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh">Karabakh</a>, from 1214 until his death in 1261. He built the monastery of Gandzasar, seat of the Catholicos of Aghvank, consecrated in 1240. He submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and kept his principality, but was later arrested and executed on the orders of a Mongol commander.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasan-jalal-dawla.jpg" alt="Hasan-Jalal Dawla" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Հայկ Ափրիկյան · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hasan-Jalalians.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
